In computer science, a null value represents a reference that points, generally intentionally, to a nonexistent or invalid {{glossary(“object”)}} or address. 
The meaning of a null reference varies among language implementations. 
In {{Glossary(“JavaScript”)}}, null is marked as one of the {{Glossary(“Primitive”, “primitive values”)}}, because its behavior is seemingly primitive. 
